01:03:37.750 --> 01:03:38.730
8.40, you're out.

1132
01:03:38.810 --> 01:03:39.950
You have an hour and 40 minutes.

1133
01:03:40.170 --> 01:03:41.870
Eat up, make your toast, get out the door.

1134
01:03:42.030 --> 01:03:45.690
And it is taking place in the Passion Package Room.

1135
01:03:46.230 --> 01:03:46.670
Wow.

1136
01:03:47.470 --> 01:03:55.630
I can tell you that we filmed all of these rehearsal dinner scenes at the famous Smokehouse restaurant in Burbank.

1137
01:03:56.130 --> 01:04:02.070
I don't know if you remember, Angela, but at the time, I lived in walking distance from the Smokehouse.

1138
01:04:02.310 --> 01:04:04.870
Oh, you were so excited when we were filming there.

1139
01:04:04.870 --> 01:04:07.870
I would walk home for lunch and I'd have lunch with Lee.

1140
01:04:08.650 --> 01:04:09.910
It was so great.

1141
01:04:10.730 --> 01:04:14.070
And guys, listen, the Smokehouse is a very famous restaurant.

1142
01:04:14.290 --> 01:04:16.810
It is right across the street from Warner Brothers Studios.

1143
01:04:17.150 --> 01:04:21.410
So a lot of like movie executives and actors eat there.

1144
01:04:21.870 --> 01:04:27.570
I guess George Clooney even named his production company after the Smokehouse restaurant.

1145
01:04:27.570 --> 01:04:31.530
Yeah, because he filmed on the Warner Brothers lot and he would walk over there.

1146
01:04:31.730 --> 01:04:33.530
That's the Hollywood lore anyway.

1147
01:04:33.970 --> 01:04:37.690
Well, the original Smokehouse only seated 46 people.

1148
01:04:38.250 --> 01:04:41.510
I found a whole little video documentary about it.

1149
01:04:41.610 --> 01:04:45.410
And I thought we should listen to a little audio clip about its history.

1150
01:04:45.850 --> 01:04:46.090
Great.

1151
01:04:47.190 --> 01:04:53.810
The original Smokehouse was started here at Riverside and Pass in Burbank in 1946 by two Lockheed engineers,

1152
01:04:54.270 --> 01:04:55.730
Jim Stockton and Jack Monroe.

1153
01:04:55.730 --> 01:04:59.170
Jim was the promoter and frontman and Jack was the cook.

1154
01:04:59.710 --> 01:05:04.170
Opening night was attended by such neighborhood luminaries as Bob Hope and Bing Crosby.

1155
01:05:04.690 --> 01:05:10.450
Soon after, all 46 seats were regularly filled to capacity and it was time to look for larger quarters.

1156
01:05:10.910 --> 01:05:15.790
As fate would have it, the Red Coach Inn, built by Danny Kaye but never opened, was available

1157
01:05:15.790 --> 01:05:19.370
and in 1948 became the permanent home of the Smokehouse.

1158
01:05:19.790 --> 01:05:23.310
By 1952, Jim's younger brother Stan was running the restaurant

1159
01:05:23.310 --> 01:05:24.670
and Chef John L.

1160
01:05:24.770 --> 01:05:30.790
Sullivan's unique recipe for garlic bread made the Smokehouse the largest purveyor of French bread west of the Mississippi.

1161
01:05:31.130 --> 01:05:35.370
Yeah, like their garlic bread was like the thing.

1162
01:05:35.630 --> 01:05:36.650
It's still the thing.

1163
01:05:36.970 --> 01:05:39.110
It brought in all the celebs.

1164
01:05:39.610 --> 01:05:43.750
I guess the new location could seat like 500 people.

1165
01:05:43.750 --> 01:05:47.430
Overall, here's a list of the people that would go to the Smokehouse for this bread.

1166
01:05:48.010 --> 01:05:51.750
Errol Flynn, Judy Garland, Robert Redford.

1167
01:05:52.270 --> 01:05:57.950
But the Smokehouse was known for respecting the privacy of celebrities.

1168
01:05:58.210 --> 01:06:00.190
They would never sell a story to the tabloids.

1169
01:06:00.890 --> 01:06:07.390
And when I first moved to Los Angeles, Angela, I had a friend who told me that once a week,

1170
01:06:07.530 --> 01:06:14.430
they would go eat lunch at the Smokehouse to try to get discovered by executives who were coming there for lunch.

1171
01:06:14.890 --> 01:06:15.970
It never happened.

1172
01:06:16.150 --> 01:06:18.570
They never got discovered.

1173
01:06:18.570 --> 01:06:22.950
I just want that guy in the ad to do something for office ladies.

1174
01:06:23.330 --> 01:06:24.350
Two gals.

1175
01:06:24.670 --> 01:06:25.390
Angela Finkley.

1176
01:06:25.770 --> 01:06:26.510
Jenna Fisher.

1177
01:06:26.810 --> 01:06:27.570
Sam Kiefer.

1178
01:06:27.910 --> 01:06:28.790
Cassie Jerkins.

1179
01:06:28.990 --> 01:06:29.630
Sitting around.

1180
01:06:30.050 --> 01:06:31.110
Talking about TV.

1181
01:06:35.270 --> 01:06:39.510
You get a sense of like the mood of the Smokehouse when you listen to that.

1182
01:06:39.670 --> 01:06:40.310
For sure.

1183
01:06:41.110 --> 01:06:43.130
Well, I think we should take a break.

